      "text": {
        "en": "Client opinions regarding veterinary staff are decidedly mixed. Many pet owners warmly praise named vets and nurses for showing compassion during end-of-life care and complex emergencies. However, other clients express deep frustration over perceived indifference, junior staff handling exotic cases, and abrupt administrative interactions."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 13,
      "title": {
        "en": "Contrasting experiences with phone communication"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Communication from the hospital divides recent reviewers significantly. While clients attending in person often commend clinicians for thorough treatment discussions, multiple emergency callers report severe difficulties reaching staff by phone. Reviewers cite unanswered calls, unreturned follow-up messages, and confusing advice."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attentive care for diverse species"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners commend the veterinary team for their skilled handling of dogs, cats, cockerels, and exotic pets during appointments. Reviewers highlight that clinicians take time to keep stressed pets comfortable during emergency examinations. Clients value having access to hospital facilities equipped to manage fragile and ill animals."
      }
    }
  ],
